      "extract": "\\label{sec:introduction} The mid 1980's saw a remarkable burst of knot invariants appearing from surprising directions; one of the foremost was the HOMPLYPT polynomial, independently discovered by several groups of researchers (see \\cite{HOMFLY,PT}). In \\cite{Jon87} this invariant was then interpreted by Jones in terms of a trace, now known as the {\\bf Jones-Ocneanu trace}, on the Hecke algebra $\\Hec_n$. In this",
